## 12. Analytics Implementation Requirements

Because integrated analytics is a major objective, investigate exactly what data the website currently collects and what it can reliably measure.

Define the measurement model before building reports.

For every important metric, document:

- Metric name.
- Business definition.
- Calculation method.
- Required events or records.
- Data source.
- Time zone.
- Attribution rules where applicable.
- Known limitations.
- Data freshness.
- Retention policy.

Implement appropriate event collection and reporting infrastructure when needed.

Support privacy-conscious measurement, consent handling where required, duplicate-event prevention, and reliable aggregation.

Distinguish between:

- Events observed by the application.
- Derived metrics calculated from those events.
- Business records such as actual orders or subscriptions.
- Imported information from connected services.
- Estimates.
- Unavailable measurements.

Do not imply that first-party tracking captures all browser activity or all external traffic sources.

Provide a clear analytics data-quality view so administrators can identify missing events, tracking failures, delayed processing, and unreliable reports.

