## 14. Execute the Rebuild in Controlled Phases

Follow this implementation sequence.

### Phase 1: Discovery

Inspect the application, identify all admin routes, review the existing architecture, and document the current capabilities.

Deliverable: A verified system inventory and initial risk assessment.

### Phase 2: Audit

Assess every module and workflow, identify bugs and usability problems, and compare current functionality against the required administrative capabilities.

Deliverable: A comprehensive audit and feature gap matrix.

### Phase 3: Architecture

Define the information architecture, module structure, permissions, data requirements, analytics model, and technical implementation strategy.

Deliverable: A clear implementation plan grounded in the actual codebase.

### Phase 4: Design System

Create or refine reusable design tokens, layout patterns, navigation, tables, forms, charts, and responsive components.

Deliverable: A consistent design system aligned with the public website.

### Phase 5: Core Rebuild

Implement the primary layout, navigation, dashboard, common interaction patterns, permissions, and essential administrative workflows.

Deliverable: A functioning foundation rather than a collection of disconnected pages.

### Phase 6: Module Implementation

Implement and integrate the applicable management, analytics, reporting, configuration, operational, and security modules.

Deliverable: A coherent and functional administrative platform.

### Phase 7: Integration

Connect each module to the appropriate APIs, database records, background processes, and external services.

Deliverable: Working end-to-end functionality.

### Phase 8: Testing

Test functionality, data correctness, security, responsiveness, accessibility, performance, and regression risks.

Deliverable: Verified workflows and a documented list of remaining limitations.

### Phase 9: Refinement

Resolve inconsistencies, simplify confusing interactions, improve performance, and refine the design based on actual use cases.

Deliverable: A polished, consistent, production-oriented experience.

### Phase 10: Final Verification

Run the available build, lint, type-checking, and test commands. Fix newly introduced errors and verify the final result.

Deliverable: A stable implementation with clear documentation and any remaining deployment requirements.

Do not stop after creating the shell, dashboard, or first few pages. Continue until the agreed scope is implemented or a genuine external dependency prevents further completion.

